# This file records external code and design influences for this project.
# New, original code is CC0-1.0 and is not listed here.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  External sources and design influences for yarnspinner-typescript. Language
  and behavior parity target: Yarn Spinner 3.2.x (algorithms and diagnostics
  mirrored; TypeScript reimplementation unless noted as a code borrow).
title: yarnspinner-typescript external sources and influences
references:
  - type: webpage
    title: Try Yarn Spinner sample stories (BranchingDialogue, Calibrations)
    authors:
      - name: Yarn Spinner Pty. Ltd.
      - name: Paris (Calibrations story)
    urls:
      - https://try.yarnspinner.dev/samples/BranchingDialogue.yarn
      - https://try.yarnspinner.dev/samples/Calibrations.yarn
    notes: >-
      Demo content, incorporated verbatim: examples/content/calibrations/
      calibrations.yarn is byte-identical to Calibrations.yarn (kept so on
      purpose — it is the fidelity target for markup/enums/functions/
      node-group playback, and carries its own in-file author attribution,
      "Written by Paris"); examples/content/crossroads/crossroads.yarn is
      BranchingDialogue.yarn verbatim apart from a provenance comment in
      its Start node. The sample files are served by the closed-source Try
      site; no explicit content license was found at the sample endpoints
      — treated as attributed demonstration use, swap-out candidates if
      that proves wrong. Accessed 2026-09-05.
  - type: webpage
    title: Try Yarn Spinner (site design — dark-theme visual language)
    authors:
      - name: Yarn Spinner Pty. Ltd.
    url: https://try.yarnspinner.dev/
    notes: >-
      Design influence for the demos' presentation (not a CSS copy):
      examples/browser/dialogue.css lifts the .dark token set's palette
      (background hsl(30 10% 8%), foreground hsl(40 15% 92%), green primary
      hsl(142 45% 42%), plum secondary hsl(330 35% 50%), border/radius/
      shadow scale) into a small hand-written stylesheet over the demo's
      own class hooks. Accessed 2026-09-05.
  - type: software
    title: yarn-spinner-runner-ts (inspiration)
    authors:
      - name: Oleksii Chekhovskyi
    urls:
      - https://github.com/oleksii-chekhovskyi/yarn-spinner-runner-ts
    notes: >-
      Prior TypeScript runner for Yarn Spinner that inspired this project.
      Not a fork and not code-incorporated: yarnspinner-typescript is an
      independent implementation, but this project's starting point, README
      structure, and feature set derive from studying that codebase.
      Accessed 2026-09-02.
  - type: software
    title: YarnSpinner
    authors:
      - name: Yarn Spinner Pty. Ltd.
      - name: Secret Lab Pty. Ltd.
      - name: Yarn Spinner contributors
    version: v3.2.2 (commit 5b3a4ff2d24e4f727e3f90fee5d8ce637474c305)
    date-released: "2026-08-11"
    license: MIT
    urls:
      - https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner
    notes: >-
      Incorporated as the conformance-corpus git submodule pinned at the
      v3.2.2 tag (test/fixtures/upstream/YarnSpinner; see the corpus
      PROVENANCE.md and the bump-upstream skill for the pin's history).
      src/compile/crc32.ts adapts YarnSpinner/CRC32.cs (standard CRC-32,
      little-endian hex formatting for implicit line IDs).
      src/compile/tagLines.ts ports YarnSpinner.Compiler/Utility.cs
      (Utility.TagLines) and the LineTaggers/ generators (ILineTagGenerator,
      RandomLineTagGenerator, DescriptiveLineTagGenerator) at v3.2.2 —
      including the Descriptive insertion/generation algorithm and message
      texts (this project keeps the preceeding-dialogue typo verbatim).
      src/markup/lineParser.ts and src/markup/builtInReplacer.ts adapt
      YarnSpinner/YarnSpinner.Markup/LineParser.cs at v3.2.2 (markup
      parity edges, 2026-09-04: duplicate-property throw per
      MarkupAttribute's Dictionary.Add, the escaped-quote string lexer's
      failed-Match fallback, the invalid-name diagnostic range, and the
      plural/ordinal `%` current-culture rendering); src/markup/types.ts
      adapts MarkupAttribute.Shift (MarkupParseResult.cs).
      src/compile/declarationFile.ts adapts the same file's
      Utility.GenerateYarnFileWithDeclarations at v3.2.2 over the port's
      VariableDeclaration shape. src/compile/upgrader.ts ports
      YarnSpinner.Compiler/Upgrader/LanguageUpgrader.cs (UpgradeJob,
      UpgradeResult/OutputFile, TextReplacement, ApplyReplacements) at
      v3.2.2, including the upgrade-type-unsupported error and the
      replacement mismatch/out-of-range error texts. Other
      compiler and runtime behavior is a parity-driven reimplementation of
      the documented upstream algorithms (string table, shadow-line
      validation, diagnostics registry), not a code borrow.
      Accessed 2026-09-02 (crc32.ts), 2026-09-03 (tagLines.ts, submodule
      mount), 2026-09-04 (declarationFile.ts, markup parity edges),
      2026-09-05 (upgrader.ts).
  - type: software
    title: YarnSpinner-Unity
    authors:
      - name: Yarn Spinner Pty. Ltd.
      - name: Yarn Spinner contributors
    version: main
    date-released: "2026-09-03"
    license: MIT
    urls:
      - https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Unity
    notes: >-
      src/compile/stringsFile.ts ports the 8-column CSV strings-file
      contract: Runtime/YarnProject/StringTableEntry.cs
      (ParseFromCSV/CreateCSV record shape and column order),
      Editor/Importers/YarnProjectImporter.cs (entry building from the
      string table — shadow-line exclusion, GenerateCommentWithLineMetadata's
      "Line metadata: " comment), and Editor/Importers/YarnImporter.cs
      GetHashString (the first-8-hex SHA-256 lock).
      Accessed 2026-09-03.
  - type: software
    title: YarnSpinner-Rust
    authors:
      - name: Yarn Spinner Pty. Ltd.
      - name: Yarn Spinner contributors
    version: main
    date-released: "2026-09-05"
    license: Apache-2.0
    urls:
      - https://github.com/YarnSpinnerTool/YarnSpinner-Rust
    notes: >-
      Design and API-shape reference for the runtime (not a code borrow).
      ADR 0002 adopts the Rust port's pull API — `continue()` returning the
      events up to the next stopping point — as the third shape between
      upstream .NET's push handlers and this project's earlier
      mutate-and-read runner; line hints ship as the Rust treatment of
      upstream's PrepareForLines (accept_line_hints → opt-in LineHintsEvent).
      src/runtime/textProvider.ts mirrors the Rust TextProvider trait's
      contract and naming (accept_line_hints, get_text, set_language,
      extend_base_language, extend_translation, are_lines_available; the
      StringTableTextProvider default; set_language null-to-base
      convention); src/runtime/dialogue.ts and src/runtime/vm.ts carry the
      option-pending naming (is_waiting_for_option_selection →
      Dialogue.isWaitingForOptionSelection); the Transcript helpers name
      their contract after Rust Dialogue::continue_. Apache-2.0 — distinct
      from the MIT C# repository above. Accessed 2026-09-05 (citation
      record; referenced across the runtime since ADR 0002).
